nwang@black.clarku.edu (Anonymous) writes:
>I took my character, a 6th level Priest down to level 6, this is by far
>my best character, so I don't want to waste him.

Don't get frustrated if your Priest dies.  There's still a lot to learn
and experience in the lower levels of the dungeon...

>1) Do I really need 2 pets?  I now have both a large cat and a small
>dog, it's kinda nice to have them help me but getting them downstais is
>a pain.

I would recommend ditching the small dog and taking the large cat with you.
You don't need two pets making kills (thus taking away potential experience)
and eating the corpses (thus eating your potential food).

>2) I have a ring a levitation, can the monsters still attack me?  And
>what kind of traps can I avoid?

All the monsters can still hit you.  You will levitate over bear traps and
pits and trap doors.  Some other traps *will* go off anyway.  Keep the
ring though, you will need it later on...

>3) After praying once, I offered a couple of corpse to my altar, the
>message were "The corpse disappears in flame" or something, what does
>that suppose to mean?

The sacrifice was successful.  (Old corpses won't be consumed in flame.)
A successful sacrifice will put you in better standing with your god,
and *may* increase your luck or get you a present. You may want to hang 
around that level and sacrifice for a while.  Good things have been known 
to happen...

>4) I also have a pick-axe, 2 magic markers (what are they good for?) and
>a mirror, how should I use them.

These are all "tools" that you a)pply.
  Pick-axe: dig through walls, break apart boulders and statues. (try it.)
  Magic markers: Write on *blank* scrolls to make new ones, or E)ngrave
                 on the floor with them.
  Mirror: a)pply in a direction to scare that monster with its reflection,
          or redirect its special attack on itself if it seems appropriate.

>And last, can I eat green mold corpse?

Well... You *can.*  But you don't want to.

